{
  "plugin_slug": "cartflows",
  "analysis_summary": {
    "phase": "phase2",
    "plugin_version": "2.2.4",
    "ir_entry_points_reviewed": 119,
    "phase1_anomalies_reviewed": 41,
    "focus": [
      "Validated the public checkout AJAX surfaces called out by Phase 1, especially coupon/cart mutation, email/login UX, and checkout file upload.",
      "Re-traced the higher-value admin mutation surfaces: REST endpoints under `admin-core/api`, role-manager capability assignment, rollback/importer flows, Tutor LMS compatibility AJAX, and SureTriggers/Woo Dynamic Flow AJAX.",
      "Collapsed Semgrep's `check_ajax_referer(..., false)` signals by checking whether invalid-nonce branches terminate before reaching a state-changing sink."
    ],
    "result": "No Patchstack-eligible true positive or evidence-backed REVIEW finding was confirmed in CartFlows 2.2.4 after direct source validation.",
    "key_observation": "The interesting public surfaces are limited to caller-owned WooCommerce checkout/session behavior or tightly constrained media uploads, while privileged admin/REST/ability paths are capability-gated and default to administrator-only access unless an administrator intentionally delegates CartFlows capabilities.",
    "tooling_notes": [
      "Phase 1 IR and 324 Semgrep results were treated as signal sources only and were revalidated against source.",
      "The Psalm SARIF artifact existed only as `{\"status\":\"error\",\"exit_code\":1}` and provided no corroborating data."
    ]
  },
  "overall_risk": "none",
  "total_findings_analyzed": 0,
  "true_positives": 0,
  "false_positives": 0,
  "needs_review": 0,
  "findings": [],
  "negative_findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "NEG-001",
      "state": "REJECTED",
      "verdict": "FP",
      "title": "Public checkout file upload is constrained to a hardcoded media allowlist and does not expose arbitrary upload or RCE",
      "entry_point_ids": [
        "ep_ajax_priv_wp_ajax_wcf_upload_checkout_file",
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_upload_checkout_file"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 57,
          "note": "The upload handler is intentionally exposed on both `wp_ajax_` and `wp_ajax_nopriv_` for checkout visitors."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-markup.php",
          "line_number": 1776,
          "note": "The file-upload nonce is localized into the public checkout page."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 295,
          "note": "The handler rejects requests without a valid `wcf-file-upload` nonce."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/classes/class-cartflows-helper.php",
          "line_number": 1933,
          "note": "The master extension allowlist is fixed to media/document types: jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp, ico, pdf, mp3, m4a, wav, mp4, m4v, mov."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 315,
          "note": "Field-level restrictions are intersected with the master allowlist before acceptance."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 331,
          "note": "The code validates extension and MIME using `wp_check_filetype_and_ext()`."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 423,
          "note": "The stored filename is replaced with `wcf_<uuid>.<ext>` via `wp_unique_filename()`."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 425,
          "note": "Upload storage goes through `wp_handle_upload()` into the normal WordPress uploads directory."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "Because the route is available to unauthenticated checkout visitors, it might permit arbitrary file upload, stored XSS via active content, or code execution.",
        "trace": "The public checkout JavaScript sends `wcf_upload_checkout_file` requests with the localized nonce. `Cartflows_Checkout_Ajax::upload_checkout_file()` then normalizes the filename, derives the extension, intersects any field-specific restriction with `Cartflows_Helper::get_allowed_file_extensions()`, checks file size, validates the real type with `wp_check_filetype_and_ext()`, and finally stores the file through `wp_handle_upload()` using a generated UUID filename in the uploads directory.",
        "defenses": "Nonce verification is enforced before any file handling. The hardcoded allowlist excludes PHP, HTML, SVG, JS, and other scriptable/executable extensions. The handler also validates MIME/extension agreement, constrains filenames to generated UUID-based names, and does not let the request control the destination path.",
        "refutation": "I tried to identify a route from user input to an executable or scriptable extension and could not. The user-controlled `checkout_id` only influences stricter field-level restrictions fetched from post meta; it does not widen the master allowlist or change the storage path.",
        "conclusion": "Rejected as a false positive for arbitrary file upload / RCE. The route is intentionally public for checkout UX, but the reachable sink is a constrained media upload under WordPress uploads semantics."
      },
      "reopen_if": "Show a bundled path that permits an executable or scriptable extension despite the master allowlist, or a path that moves the uploaded file outside the normal uploads directory."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "NEG-002",
      "state": "REJECTED",
      "verdict": "FP",
      "title": "Public checkout AJAX surfaces stay inside the caller's checkout session; helper endpoints do not become a practical auth bypass",
      "entry_point_ids": [
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_woo_apply_coupon",
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_woo_remove_coupon",
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_woo_remove_cart_product",
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_check_email_exists",
        "ep_ajax_nopriv_wp_ajax_nopriv_wcf_woocommerce_login"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 45,
          "note": "Coupon, cart, email-check, and login helpers are deliberately registered for public checkout visitors."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 123,
          "note": "`apply_coupon()` reaches `WC()->cart->add_discount(...)` after nonce validation."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 171,
          "note": "`wcf_woo_remove_cart_product()` reads the item from the current `WC()->cart` session and removes that cart item."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/assets/js/checkout-template.js",
          "line_number": 628,
          "note": "The public checkout UI intentionally calls `wcf_check_email_exists` to decide whether to show the login prompt."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 211,
          "note": "`check_email_exists()` returns only `email_exists()` plus the checkout-login-reminder flag."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/assets/js/checkout-template.js",
          "line_number": 724,
          "note": "The public checkout login form intentionally posts to `wcf_woocommerce_login`."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/modules/checkout/classes/class-cartflows-checkout-ajax.php",
          "line_number": 273,
          "note": "`woocommerce_user_login()` delegates to normal WordPress `wp_signon()` authentication after nonce validation."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "The nopriv checkout AJAX routes might expose state-changing or authentication-impacting behavior beyond the current visitor's checkout context.",
        "trace": "Coupon application and cart-item removal operate directly on `WC()->cart`, which is session-scoped to the current visitor. The email-check helper returns whether an email exists so the checkout can decide whether to show a login prompt. The login helper simply forwards the supplied credentials into `wp_signon()` and then reloads the page on success.",
        "defenses": "The routes are intentionally public because checkout itself is public. Coupon/cart routes require their own checkout nonces and operate on the caller's current WooCommerce session, not on another user's stored order or account. The login route still uses normal WordPress authentication semantics through `wp_signon()`.",
        "refutation": "I did not find any path that lets a visitor mutate another user's cart or account state. The email-existence response does disclose account existence on the checkout page, but from the plugin code alone that is a low-grade UX signal rather than a meaningful privilege boundary break, account takeover path, or Patchstack-eligible issue.",
        "conclusion": "Rejected as a reportable security finding. These endpoints implement the intended guest-checkout flow rather than exposing a cross-user state change or authentication bypass."
      },
      "reopen_if": "Show a path from these public helpers to cross-user cart manipulation, credential bypass, or another concrete security impact beyond account-existence feedback."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "NEG-003",
      "state": "REJECTED",
      "verdict": "FP",
      "title": "Tutor LMS course-template save AJAX is properly nonce- and object-capability-gated",
      "entry_point_ids": [
        "ep_ajax_priv_wp_ajax_cartflows_save_tutor_course_template"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/compatibilities/plugins/tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php",
          "line_number": 58,
          "note": "The save action is registered only on the authenticated `wp_ajax_` hook."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/compatibilities/plugins/tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php",
          "line_number": 104,
          "note": "The nonce is localized only on the Tutor course-builder admin page."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/compatibilities/plugins/tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php",
          "line_number": 200,
          "note": "`ajax_save_course_template()` verifies the request nonce before any write."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/compatibilities/plugins/tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php",
          "line_number": 217,
          "note": "The handler requires `current_user_can( 'edit_post', $course_id )` for the targeted course."
        },
        {
          "file_path": "plugins/cartflows/compatibilities/plugins/tutor-lms/class-cartflows-tutor-compatibility.php",
          "line_number": 228,
          "note": "Only after both checks does it write the selected template to course meta."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "Phase 1 flagged a missing-capability condition on the Tutor LMS course-template AJAX write.",
        "trace": "The authenticated AJAX callback verifies the Tutor-specific nonce, validates the supplied course ID, enforces `edit_post` on that exact course object, sanitizes and validates the template ID, and then stores the result with `update_post_meta()`.",
        "defenses": "The nonce is minted only for the course-builder page, and the capability check is object-specific rather than a broad role check.",
        "refutation": "I could not find a lower-privileged or unauthenticated branch that reaches the `update_post_meta()` sink without satisfying `current_user_can( 'edit_post', $course_id )`.",
        "conclusion": "Rejected as a false positive. The suspected missing-capability path is refuted by the live nonce and object-capability checks."
      },
      "reopen_if": "Show a bundled path where a user who cannot edit the target Tutor course can still reach `update_post_meta()` for `Cartflows_Tutor_Compatibility::META_KEY`."
    },
